Singleton: (3, 4); normalized false; sweeps 0. Zero iterations with two vertices: x coordinates -1, 1; normalized true.
\image(figures/force_directed_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Repeated edge records strengthen attraction. Loops are visited but ignored by the force law. Below the table, executed coincidence, singleton and zero-sweep controls expose their distinct normalization behavior.)
\alttext(A native bar chart shows negative first-vertex net force without edges, weaker negative force with one edge, positive force with three repeated attractive records and the same force as one edge when loops are added.)

With n<2 the original API returns seeded positions immediately; a singleton is not
moved to the origin and ignores even an enormous sweep request. Supplied-position
variants preserve the same early return. With n>=2, zero sweeps still center and
scale. Thus empty, singleton and zero-iteration cases are separate contracts.
The pre-existing edge-versus-isolated-distance test is a property of its particular
seeded control graph, not a universal guarantee about every adjacent pair or layout.
Different seeds can produce different drawings, and the API promises neither a
unique embedding nor minimum crossings, edge length, stress or potential.

> Actual work and complete trace admission

For n>=2 and M nonloop records, T sweeps visit T*n*(n−1)/2 repulsive pairs,
T*E edge records (including ignored loops), T*M attractions and T*n vertex moves.
Validation and initialization add O(n+E), so total direct work is
O(n+E+T*(n squared+E+n)); ordinary output and scratch use O(n) extra storage.
The native complete-graph generator supplies the dense control below. Sparse
attraction does not remove the all-pairs repulsion cost. These counts measure
executed visits, not wall-clock time or cross-library performance.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/force_directed_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/force_directed_layout.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <print>
#include <iostream>
#include <limits>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> x,pairs,attractions;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  std::print("| vertices | edge records | pair visits | attraction visits | moves |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{2u,4u,8u,16u,32u}){const auto edges=dm::algorithms::complete_graph_edges(n);const auto w=dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_work(n,edges,10,7).work;std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,edges.size(),w.pair_visits,w.attraction_visits,w.vertex_moves);x.push_back(double(x.size()));pairs.push_back(double(w.pair_visits));attractions.push_back(double(w.vertex_moves));labels.push_back(std::to_string(n));}
  const auto bound=dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace_entries(2,1,2);bool quota=false,domain=false,overflow=false,huge=false;
  try{dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace(2,{{0,1}},2,7,bound-1);}catch(const std::length_error&){quota=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace_from({{0,0},{std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),0}},{{0,1}},2,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){domain=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_from({{-1e200,0},{1e200,0}},{{0,1}},1);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace_entries(std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max(),0);}catch(const std::length_error&){huge=true;}
  std::vector<dm::algorithms::Point2D> initial{{-.25,0},{.25,0}};std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> edges{{0,1}};const auto t=dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace_from(initial,edges,2,bound);initial[0].x=99;edges.clear();const bool owned=t.initial[0].x==-.25&&t.edges.size()==1;
  std::print("\nWhole trace entries {}; one below rejected {}; exact bound frames {}; original 500-sweep bound {}.\n",bound,quota,t.frames.size(),dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace_entries(4,3,500));
  std::print("Checked controls: domain before quota {}; finite attraction overflow {}; virtual full-width bound {}; owned after caller edits {}.\n",domain,overflow,huge,owned);
  std::print("Empty and singleton full-width-sweep bounds: {}, {}.\n",dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace_entries(0,0,std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max()),dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout_trace_entries(1,0,std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max()));
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,pairs,"Pair visits",{220,38,38},2).points(x,pairs,"",{220,38,38},4).lines(x,attractions,"Vertex moves",{37,99,235},2).points(x,attractions,"",{37,99,235},4).x_tick_labels(labels).legend({"Repulsion pair visits","Vertex moves"},{{220,38,38},{37,99,235}}).title("Actual direct work for ten sweeps").xlab("Vertices; consecutive powers of two").ylab("Completed visits; linear count scale").size(950,520).save_svg("build/force_directed_work.svg");
  if(!quota||!domain||!overflow||!huge||!owned)throw std::runtime_error("checked capture controls");
}
